                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c12f768-db17-49fb-96f8-e02111c04e4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "8a7c2697-4ebb-38ed-8ea7-220aa2c67eca",
                        "target_lang_word": "inspire",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inspire",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59e6635e-10d2-3283-b613-2238f910a0ba",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To infuse into the mind; to communicate to the spirit; to convey, as by a divine or supernatural influence; to disclose preternaturally; to produce in, as by inspiration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "247da61d-0e3e-476b-ba81-a7f577505271",
                                                "sense_id": "59e6635e-10d2-3283-b613-2238f910a0ba",
                                                "text": "He knew not his Maker, and him that inspired into him an active soul."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1538294a-7900-4cbb-9fa3-62bfeb0f058e",
                                                "sense_id": "59e6635e-10d2-3283-b613-2238f910a0ba",
                                                "text": "Dawning day new comfort hath inspired."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24ebd86f-67be-4e5c-b62a-f692d84f2d22",
                                                "sense_id": "59e6635e-10d2-3283-b613-2238f910a0ba",
                                                "text": "Last spring, the periodical cicadas emerged across eastern North America. Their vast numbers and short above-ground life spans inspired awe and irritation in humans—and made for good meals for birds and small mammals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05a05c89-22d9-386f-8af9-170b94a2ad1f",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To infuse into; to affect, as with a superior or supernatural influence; to fill with what animates, enlivens or exalts; to communicate inspiration to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7414c59e-0313-4bd4-9ccb-b38625d69048",
                                                "sense_id": "05a05c89-22d9-386f-8af9-170b94a2ad1f",
                                                "text": "Elders should inspire children with sentiments of virtue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6a99ffa-9c6b-4541-a82e-c15f020a0e3a",
                                                "sense_id": "05a05c89-22d9-386f-8af9-170b94a2ad1f",
                                                "text": "The captain's speech was aimed to inspire her team to victory in the final."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85aa2513-25a3-4d06-872a-e835971d6311",
                                                "sense_id": "05a05c89-22d9-386f-8af9-170b94a2ad1f",
                                                "text": "Erato, thy poet's mind inspire, / And fill his soul with thy celestial fire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ee94086-4c35-3f22-9e61-628a01256a9c",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To draw in by the operation of breathing; to inhale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ab6d183-ad3d-476a-a72a-9397a63d799b",
                                                "sense_id": "6ee94086-4c35-3f22-9e61-628a01256a9c",
                                                "text": "By means of those sulfurous coal smokes the lungs are as it were stifled and extremely oppressed, whereby they are forced to inspire and expire the air with difficulty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abd23578-5bd2-38e5-b143-7b33e37dac89",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To infuse by breathing, or as if by breathing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d80968b2-fdbf-3f29-a24e-3018a3c8b0d1",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To breathe into; to fill with the breath; to animate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfb69708-066c-4cac-9e0d-3bd91be4e57d",
                                                "sense_id": "d80968b2-fdbf-3f29-a24e-3018a3c8b0d1",
                                                "text": "Deſcend ye nine! deſcend and ſing; / The breathing inſtruments inſpire, / VVake into voice each ſilent ſtring, / And ſvveep the ſounding lyre!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec390e46-771e-3093-ad29-03076f24f6dd",
                                        "entry_id": "71613800-59f5-3246-bc3c-42c41f78cff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spread rumour indirectly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
